Task 3: Implement Backup, Recovery, and Monitoring Strategies
Subtask 3.1: Configure Satellite Backup
Set up comprehensive backup strategies for the Satellite server.

# Install backup utilities
dnf install -y satellite-maintain

# Create backup directory
mkdir -p /backup/satellite

# Create backup script
cat > /root/satellite_backup.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

BACKUP_DIR="/backup/satellite"
DATE=$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)
BACKUP_PATH="${BACKUP_DIR}/satellite_backup_${DATE}"

# Create backup directory
mkdir -p ${BACKUP_PATH}

# Perform offline backup
satellite-maintain backup offline ${BACKUP_PATH}

# Compress backup
tar -czf ${BACKUP_PATH}.tar.gz -C ${BACKUP_DIR} satellite_backup_${DATE}

# Remove uncompressed backup
rm -rf ${BACKUP_PATH}

# Keep only last 7 backups
find ${BACKUP_DIR} -name "satellite_backup_*.tar.gz" -mtime +7 -delete

echo "Backup completed: ${BACKUP_PATH}.tar.gz"
EOF

chmod +x /root/satellite_backup.sh

# Schedule daily backups
echo "0 2 * * * /root/satellite_backup.sh" | crontab -
Subtask 3.2: Configure Database Backup
Set up PostgreSQL database backup procedures.

# Create database backup script
cat > /root/db_backup.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

BACKUP_DIR="/backup/database"
DATE=$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)

mkdir -p ${BACKUP_DIR}

# Backup Foreman database
sudo -u postgres pg_dump foreman > ${BACKUP_DIR}/foreman_${DATE}.sql

# Backup Candlepin database
sudo -u postgres pg_dump candlepin > ${BACKUP_DIR}/candlepin_${DATE}.sql

# Backup Pulp database
sudo -u postgres pg_dump pulpcore > ${BACKUP_DIR}/pulpcore_${DATE}.sql

# Compress backups
gzip ${BACKUP_DIR}/*_${DATE}.sql

# Keep only last 14 days
find ${BACKUP_DIR} -name "*.sql.gz" -mtime +14 -delete

echo "Database backups completed for ${DATE}"
EOF

chmod +x /root/db_backup.sh

# Schedule database backups
echo "30 1 * * * /root/db_backup.sh" | crontab -l | { cat; echo "30 1 * * * /root/db_backup.sh"; } | crontab -
Subtask 3.3: Set Up Recovery Procedures
Create recovery procedures and test restoration processes.

# Create recovery script
cat > /root/satellite_recovery.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

if [ $# -ne 1 ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <backup_file.tar.gz>"
    exit 1
fi

BACKUP_FILE=$1
RESTORE_DIR="/tmp/satellite_restore"

# Extract backup
mkdir -p ${RESTORE_DIR}
tar -xzf ${BACKUP_FILE} -C ${RESTORE_DIR}

# Stop Satellite services
satellite-maintain service stop

# Restore from backup
satellite-maintain restore ${RESTORE_DIR}/satellite_backup_*

# Start services
satellite-maintain service start

echo "Recovery completed from ${BACKUP_FILE}"
EOF

chmod +x /root/satellite_recovery.sh

# Create recovery documentation
cat > /root/RECOVERY_PROCEDURES.md << 'EOF'
# Satellite Recovery Procedures

## Full System Recovery
1. Install fresh RHEL system
2. Install Satellite packages
3. Run recovery script: `/root/satellite_recovery.sh <backup_file>`

## Database Recovery
1. Stop Satellite services: `satellite-maintain service stop`
2. Restore databases from SQL dumps
3. Start services: `satellite-maintain service start`

## Configuration Recovery
- SSL certificates: `/root/ssl-build/`
- Custom configurations: `/etc/foreman/`
- Puppet modules: `/etc/puppetlabs/code/`
EOF
